  "description": "Bounded simulator subset of the official Amazon AppStream API (2016-12-01). Every other official operation returns HTTP 501 UnknownOperationException. Stacks, app blocks and applications are configuration metadata: no fleet, image, image builder, app block builder, streaming instance, streaming URL, user or session exists. CreateFleet, CreateImageBuilder, CreateStreamingURL, AssociateFleet and the other provisioning and streaming APIs return UnknownOperationException with HTTP 501. App blocks stay INACTIVE and no virtual hard disk, setup script or icon is read from Amazon S3; CUSTOM app blocks require SetupScriptDetails and applications report no IconURL. Storage connectors, access endpoints, embed host domains and application settings are stored without creating buckets, endpoints or identity provider links. UpdateStack DeleteStorageConnectors and AttributesToDelete, and UpdateApplication AttributesToDelete, are refused. Applications must reference a live app block, but deleting an app block does not check the applications that reference it. Entitlements, directory configurations (which hold service account passwords), themes and usage report subscriptions return HTTP 501.",
